{
  "name": "NDIS Claims — API Submission (Simulated)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "ed9fd2c2-0b28-4d19-bd96-1bdfe71c1949",
      "name": "Run API Submission",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "153bc915-3c62-48dd-ad64-8a60c0a60000",
      "name": "Fetch Validated Agency Claims",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "row",
        "operation": "get",
        "dataTableId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "EMFKNhToLz6JUFat",
          "cachedResultName": "ndis_claims_ledger"
        },
        "matchType": "allConditions",
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "keyName": "status",
              "condition": "eq",
              "keyValue": "validated"
            },
            {
              "keyName": "plan_type",
              "condition": "eq",
              "keyValue": "agency"
            },
            {
              "keyName": "batch_id",
              "condition": "eq",
              "keyValue": "BATCH-API-DEMO"
            }
          ]
        },
        "returnAll": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "34a2ca88-b74f-4a51-8f4a-58c6e4e7e1a0",
      "name": "Build Payment Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        440,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "\nconst claims = $input.all().map(i => i.json);\nif (!claims.length) return [];\n\nconst payload = claims.map(c => ({\n  claim_reference: c.claim_reference,\n  invoice_number: c.invoice_number,\n  ndis_number: c.ndis_number,\n  support_item_number: c.support_item_number,\n  service_date: c.service_date,\n  quantity: Number(c.quantity) || 1,\n  unit_price: Number(c.unit_price) || 0,\n  total: Number(c.total) || 0\n}));\n\nreturn [{ json: { batch_id: 'API-' + $today.toFormat('yyyyLLdd'), claims: payload } }];\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "22e65e2b-c0cc-4a22-8033-96a6a0850593",
      "name": "Submit Payment Requests (NDIA API)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        660,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://YOUR_N8N_INSTANCE/webhook/ndia-mock/payment-requests",
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "json",
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ $json }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyHeaders": "keypair",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Accept",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0abcc8d8-06ba-4876-b497-6d9d7768022c",
      "name": "Apply Outcomes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        880,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "\nconst res = $input.first().json;\nconst results = Array.isArray(res.results) ? res.results : [];\n\nconst out = [];\nfor (const r of results) {\n  const status = String(r.status || '').toLowerCase();\n  const paid = status.includes('paid') || status.includes('accept') || status.includes('success');\n  out.push({ json: {\n    claim_reference: r.claim_reference,\n    outcome: paid ? 'paid' : 'rejected',\n    payment_request_number: r.payment_request_number || '',\n    paid_amount: paid ? (Number(r.paid_amount) || 0) : 0,\n    paid_date: paid ? $today.toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd') : '',\n    rejection_reason: paid ? '' : (r.error_message || 'Rejected by NDIA')\n  }});\n}\nreturn out;\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1d9fdceb-9c96-4610-9f9b-59435e60ccbf",
      "name": "Update Ledger Outcome",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "row",
        "operation": "update",
        "dataTableId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "EMFKNhToLz6JUFat",
          "cachedResultName": "ndis_claims_ledger"
        },
        "matchType": "allConditions",
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "keyName": "claim_reference",
              "condition": "eq",
              "keyValue": "={{ $json.claim_reference }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "matchingColumns": [
            "claim_reference"
          ],
          "schema": [],
          "value": {
            "status": "={{ $json.outcome }}",
            "paid_amount": "={{ $json.paid_amount }}",
            "paid_date": "={{ $json.paid_date }}",
            "rejection_reason": "={{ $json.rejection_reason }}"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "35f54772-fe93-4a58-8bc1-a550d8ec8df8",
      "name": "Build Submission Summary",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1320,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "\nconst rows = $('Apply Outcomes').all().map(i => i.json);\nconst paid = rows.filter(r => r.outcome === 'paid');\nconst rejected = rows.filter(r => r.outcome === 'rejected');\n\nlet paidTotal = 0;\nfor (const p of paid) { paidTotal += Number(p.paid_amount) || 0; }\npaidTotal = Math.round(paidTotal * 100) / 100;\n\nlet html = '<h2>NDIS claims submitted via API</h2>';\nhtml += '<p>Submitted ' + rows.length + ' claims directly to the NDIA payment request API. <b>' + paid.length + '</b> paid totalling <b>$' + paidTotal.toFixed(2) + '</b>, <b>' + rejected.length + '</b> rejected. No CSV, no portal upload, no results file - outcomes were applied to the ledger automatically.</p>';\n\nif (rejected.length) {\n  html += '<h3>Rejected — resubmission queue</h3><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Reason</th></tr>';\n  for (const r of rejected) { html += '<tr><td>' + r.claim_reference + '</td><td>' + r.rejection_reason + '</td></tr>'; }\n  html += '</table>';\n}\n\nreturn [{ json: { html: html, paid_count: paid.length, rejected_count: rejected.length, paid_total: paidTotal.toFixed(2) } }];\n"
      },
      "executeOnce": true
    },
    {
      "id": "e059d705-f417-41c5-8a09-09028d9cdf76",
      "name": "Email API Submission Summary",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        1540,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "message",
        "operation": "send",
        "sendTo": "admin@example.com",
        "subject": "=NDIS API submission: {{ $json.paid_count }} paid (${{ $json.paid_total }}), {{ $json.rejected_count }} rejected",
        "emailType": "html",
        "message": "={{ $json.html }}",
        "options": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "webhookId": "3a1a798a-5ce6-44a0-8b94-48fd40348c34"
    },
    {
      "id": "10c77947-45db-4626-a97f-bb2e77ef17d2",
      "name": "Sticky Note d32577e8",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## The API future-state path (simulated)\n\nWhat the whole claims round-trip looks like WITH NDIA Digital Partnership Office access: validated agency claims go from the ledger straight to the NDIA payment request API and outcomes come back in the same run — replacing the CSV email, the PRODA portal upload, the results file download, and the reconciliation form entirely.\n\nCurrently pointed at the in-instance mock (NDIA API Simulator workflow). To go real once DPO access is granted: change the URL in 'Submit Payment Requests' to the NDIA endpoint and attach the machine-to-machine PRODA credential. Nothing else changes.",
        "color": 3
      }
    }
